    {
      "id": "sum-c6c57c",
      "kind": "evolution",
      "body": "Wording moved from 'avoid or protect' to concrete type-allowlisting, then to an explicit ban on known-insecure mechanisms, then dropped the BinaryFormatter example, then widened scope from clients to any untrusted data. Level went L1 to L2 in #2694. The v5 ID V1.5.2 coincidentally reuses a v4 number from the merged architecture requirement.",
